    "result_text": "All 65 tests pass. BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event in `OwnerRestControllerV1.createOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`).\n\n**What was added**, right after the existing human-readable audit line:\n\n- A process-wide `AtomicLong AUDIT_EVENT_SEQ` that yields a monotonically increasing `seq` across all creates.\n- A static Jackson 3 `ObjectMapper` (`JsonMapper`) used to serialize the event to compact JSON.\n- Emission of an immutable JSON event on the `AUDIT` logger:\n\n  ```json\n  {\"seq\":52,\"ownerId\":62,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-AC59B6E2\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n  ```\n\nDesign points matching the spec:\n- **Immutable**: the event is built in a local `LinkedHashMap` and emitted as a serialized JSON string \u2014 nothing mutable is retained or shared.\n- **Monotonic `seq`**: an `AtomicLong.incrementAndGet()` guarantees a strictly increasing integer across concurrent creates.\n- **Current primary identifier**: the `customerCode` field carries `owner.getCustomerCode()` \u2014 the owner's present primary identifier. I noted inline (via comment) that when the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, this field will carry the memberId instead, keeping the event on the current primary identifier as later checkpoints require.\n\nThe new `Cp53Tests` passes, and the full suite is green (65/65).",
